{"name":"Galaxea","hex":"#2e305e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Galaxea","blocks":[{"text":"Galaxea is a genus of colonial stony corals in the family Euphylliidae. Common names include crystal, galaxy, starburst and tooth coral. They are abundant on reefs in the Indo-Pacific region and the Red Sea. They are found in water less than 20 metres (66 ft) deep and favour turbid sites. They are sometimes kept in reef aquaria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Coral_%28Galaxea_fascicularis%29%2C_mar_Rojo%2C_Egipto%2C_2023-04-18%2C_DD_65.jpg/330px-Coral_%28Galaxea_fascicularis%29%2C_mar_Rojo%2C_Egipto%2C_2023-04-18%2C_DD_65.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galaxea","wikidata":"Q3094518"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"ADAC-Zentrale, Munich, March 2017-05","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/ADAC-Zentrale%2C_Munich%2C_March_2017-05.jpg/500px-ADAC-Zentrale%2C_Munich%2C_March_2017-05.jpg","ratio":1.4909165978530141,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ADAC-Zentrale,_Munich,_March_2017-05.jpg","share":0.06375},{"title":"Innenhafen Duisburg Blaue Stunde 2014","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg/500px-Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg","ratio":1.6818845872899928,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg","share":0.04875},{"title":"Silhouette of an island at dusk with blue clouds in Don Det Si Phan Don Laos","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Silhouette_of_an_island_at_dusk_with_blue_clouds_in_Don_Det_Si_Phan_Don_Laos.jpg/500px-Silhouette_of_an_island_at_dusk_with_blue_clouds_in_Don_Det_Si_Phan_Don_Laos.jpg","ratio":1.5998238402818556,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silhouette_of_an_island_at_dusk_with_b